  "diagnostic": {
    "method": "An independent diagnostic release build counts admission and ordinary work at each site; verification semantics match the timed binary on the same original words. These readings were collected on the precursor which charged admitted setup at the beginning of the quantifier and had no 24-hop cap on singleton-wrapper recognition. The study formulas have fewer wrappers. Completed batches incur the same charge on the final implementation. For an unfinished batch, the recorded diagnostic charge is specific to that diagnostic build. All formulas use the original 1M work limit. Counts only describe operations that actually occurred before a stop.",
    "columns": [
      "membership atom absent positions handled via index",
      "membership atom stored positive positions",
      "sparse fairness occurrence positions skipped",
      "sparse fairness occurrence positions admitted before the subscript test",
      "sparse fairness cycle enabledness positions skipped",
      "sparse fairness cycle enabledness positions evaluated",
      "ordinary temporal atom positions charged"
    ],
    "binding": "Formula IDs are per bound IR. On the original source, 844 is forall c in ElevatorCall: SF_Vars(DispatchElevator(c)); 254 is TemporalInvariant including its quantified existential response. Source mutation can change IDs. An individual dense key or the priming binding may still take the ordinary path.",
    "reproduction": "Inside evaluate_lasso record formula.expr.index(), states.len() and Word.cells on return. At each successful indexed leaf record n-positions.len() and positions.len(); at sparse_fairness record the same two values at occurrence, then n-back_to-cycle.len() and cycle.len() before fair_enabled. In the ordinary leaf path count n after successful charge. Reset counters for each formula.",
